[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "french-open 2.d4"]
[Name "2...c6: ...d5 one move late"]

2... c6 { Black has played the c-pawn to c6 and will want ...c5 later, so this costs a move. }
3. Bd3 { Guards e4, as against every other second move. }
3... d5 { Now it is a French with the pawn on c6. }
4. Nd2 { The same knight move, the same plan. }
4... Nf6
5. e5 Nfd7
6. Ne2 { The same set-up as in the Closed Tarrasch. }
6... c5
7. c3 Nc6
8. O-O { The position of the Closed Tarrasch, but with White a whole move ahead, because Black's c-pawn took two moves to get here. White scores over 60%. [%idea castle-early] } *
